Of course. I understand the "too many re-renders" issue (React error #310) is persistent, particularly when interacting with the "Add New Profile" feature in the `DieModal`. I also acknowledge the critical issue with the "Process Log Sheet" inputs.

I have found the specific cause for the infinite loop: a synchronous state update (`setForm`) inside a `useEffect` that is triggered by a parent state change (`addProfile` result). I will fix this by using a dedicated `useEffect` to handle the post-creation selection asynchronously.

I will also apply the permanent fix for the Process Log Sheet by moving the helper components outside the main component scope.

Here is the corrected code.

# Updated files:

## pages/DiesAndPlanning.tsx

Refactored `DieModal` in `DiesAndPlanning.tsx` to fix the infinite re-render loop (React error #310). The logic for selecting a newly created profile has been updated to use a dedicated `useEffect` hook that runs only when `newlyCreatedProfileId` changes, breaking the synchronous update cycle. Additionally, `TempInput` and `ParamInput` components have been moved outside the main component to prevent re-creation on every render, permanently fixing the input focus loss bug.

